module scf/story_casida
  The excitation energies of water in the 6-31G basis, at the size of
  posts/2026-09-25-casida-tdhf-and-tda-for-water.viv: 13 basis functions, 5
  doubly occupied orbitals and 8 virtual ones, so 40 occupied-virtual pairs.
  The ground state comes from lib/hf with the post's options; lib/hf/casida
  moves the integrals to the orbitals, builds the Casida matrices and solves
  them both ways, for singlets and for triplets.

<main>  @5b10adab
  what             Compute the RHF ground state of water in 6-31G, its
                   orbital energies and its two-electron integrals over
                   orbitals, and from them the singlet and triplet
                   excitation energies in the Tamm-Dancoff approximation and
                   in time-dependent Hartree-Fock. The lowest of each are
                   PySCF's
                   [test "the lowest singlet is PySCF's 0.344073896628 Ha in TDHF and 0.346160646268 in TDA, to 1e-8"].
  CW_PYSCF_E       PySCF's RHF energy of this molecule in this basis, hartree
  cw_mol           water: the oxygen at the origin, the hydrogens at $y = \pm 0.757$ Å, $z = 0.587$ Å, with the 6-31G basis functions on each atom
  cw_setup         the integrals over basis functions and the electron counts: everything the SCF and the Casida matrices start from
  cw_rhf           the RHF ground state: its energy, orbitals and density
  cw_mo            the orbital energies, the integrals over orbitals, and the numbers of occupied and virtual orbitals
  cw_singlet       the singlet excitation energies, TDA and TDHF, hartree
  cw_triplet       the triplet excitation energies, TDA and TDHF, hartree
  CW_HARTREE_EV    electronvolts per hartree
  cw_e_rhf         the RHF energy, hartree
  cw_singlet_tdhf  the lowest singlet excitation energy in TDHF
  cw_singlet_tda   the lowest singlet excitation energy in TDA
  cw_triplet_tdhf  the lowest triplet excitation energy in TDHF
  cw_triplet_tda   the lowest triplet excitation energy in TDA
  cw_singlet_ev    the lowest singlet in TDHF, in electronvolts: ultraviolet light

cw_ground  @999c9526
  how    lib/hf's SCF with its default options. The default guess runs an
         SCF of its own on the spin-averaged density, which for closed-shell
         water is already the answer, so the loop that follows only confirms
         it in a few passes.
  why    Every excitation energy is computed from this state's orbitals, so
         the state must be the converged RHF one: its energy is PySCF's
         [hold "the RHF energy is PySCF's"].
  p      the setup: integrals over basis functions and electron counts
  r      the SCF result
  e      its energy, hartree

  scf    solve the RHF equations from the default guess, and keep the energy for the check
    run  The energy is {e} hartree.
